xnu 0205: the submission logs before it touches the CP

The 0204 boot is healthy up to the first client draw: `cp memwrite canary
0x600dc0de`, `cp ib canary 0x1b00dead int 0x0` and `cp uc stress 2000
refused 0` all pass, `MondrianGPU` publishes, and then the ring stops at a
frame select with no `MondrianGPU: submit flags` and no `uc pre`.

`uc pre` is built from four CPU reads of CP registers. A CP that has wedged
makes such a read never return, so the line that would name the wedge is
lost with the read that was going to name it. Print and flush `uc enter`
before the first read: if it is the last line, the wedge is in those reads;
if it never appears, the submission stopped before the driver was called.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -3251,6 +3251,11 @@
 	ring = (uint32_t *)mondrian_cp_ring.va;
 	if (dwords > 16 && mondrian_uc_logged < 8) {
 		mondrian_uc_logged++;
+		/* Before the first register read: a wedged CP makes that read
+		 * never return, and the line that names it is then lost. */
+		printf("MONDRIAN GPU: uc enter %u at 0x%x\n", dwords,
+		    mondrian_uc_at);
+		mondrian_log_flush_now();
 		printf("MONDRIAN GPU: uc pre %u at 0x%x rptr 0x%x wptr 0x%x int 0x%x bv 0x%x\n",
 		    dwords, mondrian_uc_at,
 		    mondrian_gpu_read(mondrian_uc_gpu, GEN7_CP_RB_RPTR * 4u),
